{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "S"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 119, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing a conv on the direct input-output edge loses capacity, whereas removing a skip/pool there is near-neutral."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 absent, edge 5 is one of only two inputs to the output node, so removing it collapses the cell to the single direct edge."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 1 is already none, removing edge 0 disconnects both intermediate nodes from the input."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual skip where no direct edge existed helps, while replacing an existing conv with skip removes capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing weak parameter-free pooling with a conv on the final edge yields a larger gain than replacing other ops."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping a learnable 3x3 conv for pooling degrades accuracy, unlike replacing none or skip."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Pool-to-conv replacement is one of the most consistently beneficial changes in NAS-Bench-201."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Downgrading a 3x3 conv to 1x1 on the direct path loses receptive field, while upgrading skip/none/pool to 1x1 does not."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the dir